## SECTION 9: THE HARD MATHEMATICS & THEMATIC INTEGRATION

### Subsection 1: The Over-Draft Formula
$$\Delta M = \frac{E_{\text{emergency}}}{\text{Efficiency Constant } (k)}$$
- Where $k = 3,500\text{ kcal per lb of human tissue}$. This equation tracks structural tissue conversion during a Level 4 Over-Draft event, mapping directly to physical decay metrics.

### Subsection 2: Core Refinement & Absorption Limit ($A_r$)
The total capacity for a human host or rival beast to metabolize and break down a Core through internal consumption follows an inverse density threshold:
$$A_r = \alpha \times (T_h)^2 \times \left(1 + \frac{S}{100}\right) \cdot \left[ \frac{Q_{\text{current}}}{Q_{\text{max}}} \right]$$
- Where $\alpha = 0.5$ is the metabolic coefficient, $T_h$ represents the track tier value, and $Q$ tracks the remaining internal energy charge of the Core. As $Q \to 0$, the crystal lattice structure weakens proportionally until structural integrity collapses completely.

### Subsection 3: Crop Viability Efficiency ($V$)
$$V = \frac{\text{Suppressant Volume } (L)}{\text{Ambient Soil Mutation Particle Count } (P_m)} \times 100\%$$
- Values $\ge 85\%$ yield Stage I. Values between $70\%\text{--}84\%$ yield Stage II. Values $< 70\%$ trigger Stage III (Full Siphon within 45 seconds).

### Subsection 4: The Core Maturation & Energy Density Formula
$$Q_{\max}(t) = Q_{\text{base}} \times \left(1 + \ln\left(\frac{t}{t_0}\right)\right) \times \eta_{\text{photo}}$$
- Where $Q_{\text{base}}$ is the core’s baseline structural capacity, $t$ is the age of the environmental grid in days, $t_0$ is the stabilization threshold (30 days), and $\eta_{\text{photo}}$ is the local hybrid photosynthetic index derived from combined solar and background radiation intake.

### Subsection 5: Kinetic Dispersion Wall Dynamics
$$Y_s = \frac{\frac{1}{2} M_b \cdot v_b^2}{\kappa \cdot W_{\text{thick}}}$$
- Calculates the exact structural force dispersion when a non-humanoid creature impacts a Sanctuary alloy wall partition ($W_{\text{thick}}$).

### Subsection 6: Subspecies Energy Transmission Gradients ($\mathbb{E}_g$)
$$\mathbb{E}_g = \Psi_{\text{base}} \times \left(1 + \Delta_{\text{subspecies}}\right)$$
- For Terrans: $\Delta_{\text{subspecies}} = 0.00$ (Uniform balance across all power mechanics).
- For Lithari: $\Delta_{\text{subspecies}} = +0.35 \text{ Kinetic Resist} / -0.15 \text{ Elemental Velocity}$
