### Subsection 7: Grid Binding Efficiency & Thermodynamic Degradation ($G_e$)
$$G_e = \left( \frac{\Phi_{\text{containment}}}{\Phi_{\text{raw}}} \right) \times e^{-\lambda (T_{\text{load}} - T_{\text{ambient}})}$$
- Where $\Phi_{\text{containment}}$ is the stabilization field metric supplied by Baseline Architects, $\lambda$ is the core's native radiation decay coefficient, and $T$ is the active thermal operating temperature during power draw.

### Subsection 8: Non-Humanoid Shell Hardening Metric ($H_s$)
$$H_s = H_{\text{base}} \times \left(1 + \ln\left(\frac{E_{\text{impact}}}{E_{\text{threshold}}}\right)\right) \cdot \mu_{\text{silicate}}$$
- Where $H_{\text{base}}$ is the native armor thickness, $E_{\text{impact}}$ is the incoming kinetic energy in Joules, $E_{\text{threshold}}$ is the initial deformation limit of the bio-alloy plating, and $\mu_{\text{silicate}}$ is the mineral saturation constant of the environment.

### Subsection 9: The Environmental Lethality Quotient ($ELQ$)
$$ELQ = \left( \frac{D_{\text{beast}} \times P_{\text{mutagen}}}{\Psi_{\text{shield}}} \right) \cdot \ln(T_{\text{class}})$$
- Where $D_{\text{beast}}$ is the predator density index, $P_{\text{mutagen}}$ is the atmospheric cell particle saturation, $\Psi_{\text{shield}}$ is the human engineering defense integrity value, and $T_{\text{class}}$ is the numeric tier scaling value of the local regional impactor class.

### Subsection 10: The Reproductive Core Inheritance Multiplier ($\mathbb{R}_m$)
When fauna engage in their natural reproductive cycles, the energy density passed down to the offspring's internal seed core is mathematically scaled by the parents' combined core maturity levels:
$$\mathbb{R}_m = \left( \frac{Q_{\text{paternal}} + Q_{\text{maternal}}}{2} \right) \times \gamma_{\text{instinct}}$$
- Where $\gamma_{\text{instinct}}$ represents the localized territorial stability coefficient ($1.0$ to $1.5$). Higher parental dominance and stable nesting environments directly yield structurally superior, higher-tier newborn seed cores, ensuring the natural selection and evolutionary advancement of the species.

